  "id": "scripted-incoming-temperature",
  "name": "Rhai · incoming-only temperature",
  "category": "Rhai boundary scripts",
  "description": "Transient thermal inlet using a scripted Inlet/outlet temperature condition.",
  "capabilities": [
    "Workbench",
    "TwoD",
    "Editable",
    "Rhai",
    "Temperature profile",
    "Transient",
    "Pre-attached script"
  ],
  "expectations": {
    "closed_domain": false,
    "positive_streamwise_flow": false,
    "curved_boundary": false,
    "non_ideal_mesh_quality": false,
    "notes": "Thermal condition: Inlet/outlet temperature. On incoming faces T=293.15+2 sin(2*pi*t) K; outgoing faces use zero gradient. The same thermal hook can be attached to an outlet with explicitly specified physical backflow velocity. No velocity backflow script is supported.\n\nOpen Setup > Boundaries > inlet > Scripts / attach profile to inspect the pre-attached code. Use Check / preview, then Attach / update to apply parameter changes. Generate a mesh before solving. Euler dt=0.01 s, 100 physical steps (1 s), with PIMPLE. Refine time step and mesh as appropriate.\n\nInitial Rhai support: Velocity inlet; static Pressure outlet (strict or explicit backflow); Fixed temperature; Inlet/outlet temperature. Heat flux, moving-wall velocity, total pressure, flow-rate, material laws and volume sources are not scripted in this release. Educational setup; not numerically validated."
  },
